# Batch files must have CRLF line endings, always.
#
# cmd.exe parses a .bat line by line and does not reliably handle bare LF: it
# mis-tokenises long lines and breaks ^ continuations outright, which surfaces as
# nonsense like "'aywright' is not recognized" — a word chopped mid-token — while
# still exiting 0. build.bat was committed LF-only and had exactly this problem,
# so pin it here rather than relying on whatever core.autocrlf happens to be set
# to on the machine doing the checkout.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
